## What changed

Documentation-only cleanup before sending the article draft externally.

- removes internal history about the earlier pooled SQLite reopen run and its rejection;
- removes wording that could imply an external reviewer performed the check;
- describes the final SQLite methodology directly in scientific terms: measured reopen uses no connection pool and the pool is cleared before measurements;
- removes code-assignment syntax such as `Pooling=False` and `ClearAllPools()` from the article prose and appendices while preserving the actual experimental condition;
- renames “corrected reopen series/experiment” to neutral “reopen series/experiment” throughout;
- keeps reproducibility facts about run id, commit, SDK, SQLite version, ordering and raw artifacts;
- removes the internal smoke-run history from the article.

No benchmark numbers, benchmark code, or scientific conclusions changed.
